WEBVTT

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.470
The whole castle's gone.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.190
This place might be wrecked,

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.030
but maybe it's for the best.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.700
Everyone looks a lot happier than 
when that lord was in charge.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.920
And it's thanks to her.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.030
Kind sirs...

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:23.740
Whoa!

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.120
I have a request for you two.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.850
Please, take Tsugumi away from the castle!

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.150
Never!

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.220
Come down, Tsugumi!

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.910
I'm not going anywhere!

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:12.190
<b>Getting Stronger</b>

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:15.060
You need to leave the Kosameda Band!

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:15.530
Don't wanna! No! No way! Lemme go!

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.320
If she wants to stay that badly, 
do you really have to kick her out?

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.090
Get down from there!

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:25.790
We aren't kicking her out. 
She needs to escape Lord Hideo.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:27.540
Escape him?

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:35.520
Lord Hideo has fallen apart after being 
betrayed by the people under his rule.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.890
Tsugumi? Where's Tsugumi...?

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.720
And because of that, he's become 
even more fixated on Tsugumi.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:42.010
Tsugumi? Tsugumi? Tsugumi!

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:47.160
If they're reunited, 
he'll try to manipulate her again.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.230
But I'm fine now!

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.870
Tsugumi...

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.200
I'm not going to do what he says anymore.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:58.700
Can you really say that for certain?

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.190
W-Well...

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.160
Listen to me, Tsugumi!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.090
As long as you stay here, 
you'll be haunted by Lord Hideo!

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:10.320
You must go! Flee the castle!

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.630
B-But... But...

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.270
The sounds of sword practice... 
The smell of the fields...

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:22.360
My memories with my sister... 
I have to leave all that behind?

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:22.580
Tsugumi...

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:26.470
I can't! I'd miss it too much!

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:28.720
She's...

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.420
I don't know if I like this.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.550
Me either.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:36.020
We'll just have to protect her 
from His Lordship this time.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.240
It's okay, Tsugumi.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.360
We'll keep you safe.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.950
Don't worry, Tsugumi.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.380
I understand. I'm going to leave the castle.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.720
Tsugumi...

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.660
She hated the idea before. 
Why'd she suddenly change her mind?

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:04.220
Hey, I don't really have any plans, 
so could I join up with you guys?

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.570
Sure, that's cool.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.630
It'll be great to have more band members.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:09.780
Thanks!

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.890
I'll go get ready.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:25.050
I already made up my mind about leaving...

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.280
You oughta get some sleep. 
We're leaving early tomorrow.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.110
You...

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:35.470
Listen, what exactly made you 
decide to leave the castle?

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.980
Because it'd be better for everyone else.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:44.350
I've let His Lordship decide 
everything for me before now.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.590
So I'm not sure I could 
really stand up to him.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.560
And if I become his puppet again,

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:56.360
instead of protecting the people in town, 
I might hurt them if he tells me to...

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.060
I don't want that to happen, ever!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:04:59.920
I see...

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.740
Pathetic, isn't it?

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:02.980
What?

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.740
The fact that I can't let go of him...

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.030
Nah. It's not pathetic at all.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.010
Isn't it hard for anyone 
to let go of their parents?

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:16.620
But we're not even related by blood. 
He's not my real father.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:18.990
I'm being weird, aren't I?

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.280
Is it really that weird...?

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:29.030
If your real parents are gone
and there's an adult to take care of you,

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.740
why wouldn't you rely on them?

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:34.930
I thought of Kojiro's dad like my own, too.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.090
I really loved him.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:39.440
Dad...

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.510
So I get how you feel.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:46.540
Really?

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:50.440
Yeah. And even though he's gone now...

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:53.940
he's the reason I have these sword
 techniques and a dream for the future.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.460
A dream for the future?

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:57.620
Don't you have anything like that?

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.600
<i>Uniting the country would be wonderful.</i>

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.260
<i>But we don't just fight for ourselves.</i>

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.840
<i>We're also doing this to protect 
people who are weaker than us.</i>

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.750
<i>That's the Bushi way, Tsugumi.</i>

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:16.640
<i>I'm gonna be a nice Bushi like you, Tsubame!</i>

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.050
I do.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:23.030
But with the way things are now...

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:25.690
I'm dependent on everyone
 instead of protecting them.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:29.440
I need to get stronger, don't I?

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.290
We're heading out. Ready?

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:42.460
We're off!

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.160
Take care!

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.630
Drop by every now and again!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:45.950
Take care of yourself!

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:45.950
Tsugumi!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.170
Thanks for everything!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.700
We're going, Tsugumi.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:50.460
Okay.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.970
Take care! Have a good trip! Goodbye!

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.230
Tsugumi!

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.420
Tsugumi! Tsugumi!

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:03.180
Tsugumi!

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.910
Don't leave!

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:09.480
Tsugumi! Make sure to come back someday!

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:10.870
You better come back!

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.720
Be sure to come visit us!

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.750
We'll be waiting for you!

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.420
Everyone...

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.480
Okay! I'm leaving for now!

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:42.930
Take care of yourselves!

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:46.890
Tsugumi! We'll be waiting!

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:49.910
Come back someday!

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:55.010
One day, when I'm strong enough 
on my own that I'm sure it'll be okay...

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:59.000
I'll return here. I'll come back home.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:04.680
I miss them!

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:08.000
Chill out. You look ridiculous 
when you're crying.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.830
We're stuck with a real handful...

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:19.450
The Bushi band we started with just
 the two of us now has a new member.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.900
The three of us are gonna 
make it the strongest ever!

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:23.740
Yeah.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:26.600
So, where are we headed next, Musashi?

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:34.210
There should be a blue Kishin up ahead.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:36.060
Let's go hunt some oni!

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.800
Who cares about hunting oni?

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:44.310
What's the point if there's no one
 to praise me for doing it?!

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:47.920
Don't you worry! We'll give you 
whatever praise you need!

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.200
You guys?

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.140
Sure!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.260
How could that possibly motivate me?!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.510
What'd you say?! You're infuriating!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.720
Hey, would you two stop moving around?!

00:08:58.720 --> 00:08:59.930
Get along with no fighting!

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.630
Yeah, you're right.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:02.610
What's that about?

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.260
It's our mantra for the trip.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.900
We get along with no fighting.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.290
Get along with no fighting.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.700
Get along with no fighting.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.300
Get along with no fighting.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.600
Get along with no fighting!

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:16.820
<i>This is gonna lead to a fight.</i>

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:22.040
I wub you, Musashi!

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:27.530
<i>Pressing her chest against me like that 
is gonna give Kojiro the wrong idea...</i>

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.700
What's going on here?!

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.750
<i>Why'd she suddenly get so clingy anyway?</i>

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.830
<i>I need to make sure 
the three of us get along.</i>

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.340
<i>You're part of the gang now!</i>

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:55.060
<i>I don't just wanna send you flying!</i>

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.580
<i>Don't you get that?</i>

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:04.750
Musashi! I don't know what to do with you!

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.910
<i>What </i>are<i> you trying to do with me?!</i>

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:09.310
<i>Why'd you strip out of the blue?!</i>

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:12.170
<i>I have no idea what goes through your head!</i>

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.080
<i>I-It's not like that, Kojiro! 
Don't give me that look!</i>

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:22.140
<i>There's nothing between me and Tsugumi!</i>

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:27.840
<i>I don't want this misunderstanding 
to cost me our ten-year friendship.</i>

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:33.370
<i>But the only way to clear it up
is to reveal an embarrassing secret...</i>

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:35.510
<i>Yes, the truth is...</i>

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.310
<i>I am definitely into older women!</i>

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:45.280
Confiscated! Confiscated! Confiscated! 
Confiscated! Confiscated! Confiscated!

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:45.280
<i>At mining school, we were subjected to a
strict lifestyle so we'd focus on mining.</i>

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:48.820
<i>Anyone caught with one of the girls 
from town would be expelled.</i>

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:53.750
Expelled! Expelled! Expelled! Expelled! 
Expelled! Expelled! Expelled!

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:53.320
<i>In other words, 
we had to suppress our desires...</i>

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.830
Get a load of Ms. Machiko, 
the phys ed teacher!

00:10:56.830 --> 00:11:01.130
She's overflowing with maternal goodness 
and curves that are just magnetic!

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:02.600
What do you think, Musashi?

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:07.020
I think I prefer Ms. Kyoko, 
the ancient texts teacher.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.000
I get you!

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:15.070
<i>We had nowhere to direct our interest 
other than the teachers...</i>

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:11.160
Tell me about it!

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:19.040
<i>But I can't tell Kojiro 
something that embarrassing!</i>

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:23.440
<i>I have to clear this up </i>and<i>
 reject Tsugumi without hurting her!</i>

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.030
<i>How am I supposed to do that?!</i>

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.450
<i>Musashi and Tsugumi 
really seem to be hitting it off...</i>

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.930
<i>I've never seen him blush like that before.</i>

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:39.270
Congratulations! I wish you all the best!

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:39.200
<i>I've been friends with 
Musashi for ten years.</i>

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.080
<i>If he's found a nice girl 
and has a shot at happiness,</i>

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:45.380
<i>I'd gladly give my blessing...</i>

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:49.260
<i>Except not! Something about this
 doesn't sit right with me at all!</i>

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:55.680
<i>And the only way I can get him to understand
is to reveal my most embarrassing secret.</i>

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:59.230
<i>I hate to admit it—I really do—because...</i>

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:04.040
<i>I have absolutely no romantic experience!</i>

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:06.540
<i>The reason being that I'm a Bushi.</i>

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:12.720
<i>What kind of girl wants a guy who gets
 looked down on and spit at every day?</i>

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:17.450
<i>Even if there were a nice girl like that, 
she'd be outcast right alongside me.</i>

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:21.930
<i>That's why I've been desperate 
to avoid women all this time...</i>

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.950
<i>But Musashi was a miner.</i>

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.140
<i>Miners got all the chicks in town.</i>

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:29.860
<i>He would've had his choice of women.</i>

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.220
Women? I think thirty...

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:34.050
No, more like forty.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:37.890
You get enough action, 
you kinda stop counting, y'know?

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:44.150
<i>If he says that, 
how will I relate to him ever again?!</i>

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:44.570
Hmph.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.860
<i>Why's Tsugumi been avoiding me, anyway?</i>

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:50.580
<i>Is it that obvious how little 
experience I have with women?</i>

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.510
<i>So she won't even look at me?</i>

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:55.710
<i>If she mentions it to Musashi, 
I don't know that I'll ever recover!</i>

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.840
<i>Anything but that!</i>

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.500
<i>I don't wanna be embarrassed!</i>

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.860
<i>I don't wanna hurt anyone!</i>

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.420
<i>Tsugumi! What the heck are you thinking?!</i>

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:09.360
<i>You have to tell us, Tsugumi! 
Just what is it...</i>

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:12.010
<i>What are you really after?!</i>

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:13.400
Will you...

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:18.640
Will you be... friends with me?

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:23.330
Uh, aren't we friends already?

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:25.360
Is that how it works?

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:29.440
I... don't actually know how 
to make friends, it turns out.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.180
What are you talking about?

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:36.920
I've never really gotten to know 
anyone outside of the Kosameda Band.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:39.560
And when I started thinking about how you two

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:42.370
are the first people I've really known 
outside of my band...

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:45.340
I-I-I-I-I didn't know what to say!

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.610
Why were you avoiding Kojiro, then?

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:52.610
I was scared he was mad at me
 for calling him the driver.

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:54.700
What, is that all?

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.800
So why'd you start stripping?

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.010
A long time ago, my sister told me...

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:02.920
<i>Tsugumi, if you ever find yourself 
unsure of what to do, take your clothes off.</i>

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:07.020
That's why! I just want 
to be friends with you guys!

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:09.030
But I'd be so embarrassed if you said no!

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:13.030
And because I didn't want to get hurt,
 I started acting weird!

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:14.360
I'm so sorry!

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.560
<i>I get you!</i>

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.350
What was that...?

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:46.960
It's morning.

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:55.430
Hey! Are you trying to eat Kojiro's sword?

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:59.750
Get back here, dammit! Drop that sword!

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.790
What's going on?

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:03.950
Your Lordship, am I on standby?
Training? A mission?

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:08.000
Kojiro's dad left that to him!

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.300
Give it back!

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:12.840
It's not some snack 
for a shrimpy oni like you!

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:17.220
Gotcha!

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:19.110
Wh-What the?!

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.570
That's nuts... This pole is made of metal!

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:27.120
It'd be one thing against a Kishin, 
but this squirt?

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:28.610
Hey! Hold it!

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:34.280
What gives? What's going on here?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.280
Dammit, dammit, dammit!

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:39.790
Why can't I win?!

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:46.410
What the heck is it doing?

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:48.860
Swords...?

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.360
There're so many. What is this place?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.310
Not bad, but...

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:18.550
Are you staring at the swords? Or at me?

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:21.380
They're all beautiful, aren't they?

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:23.050
Y-Yeah...

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:25.820
You wanna borrow one?

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:28.920
It should let you beat that oni.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.500
Otherwise... it's snack time.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:36.510
It's eating Kojiro's sword!

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:37.770
Thanks, man!

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:42.190
What is this?!

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.630
What?!

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.110
<i>It's like my arm is on fire!</i>

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:17.630
Cut it!

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.130
Cut it?

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:20.340
That's right!

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:21.850
I can cut it!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:42.420
That was crazy... 
What's up with this katana?!

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:46.160
Very nice! Was that your 
first time using one?

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.240
A Kitetsu Blade.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:50.310
This is called a Kitetsu Blade?

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:54.160
The iron sand's being drawn to the sword...

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:57.350
This is just like what the Takeda Band did.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:01.580
<i>So this is what it's like to slay an oni...</i>

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.490
<i>It feels good.</i>

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.690
Sorry! I broke it!

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:16.280
Aw, don't worry about it.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:18.710
I didn't need her.

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:21.710
She was a waste of steel, in other words.

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:24.560
You managed to draw out some 
incredible power, though...

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:25.710
I wonder why.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:30.160
Could you be the one?

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:35.140
I thought maybe, but I'm not so sure.

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:37.910
Thought what?

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.410
Master.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.450
It's time.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:47.650
Okay.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:54.320
You've made a mess again.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:58.400
Why do you insist on making patterns 
in the ground with Kitetsu Blades?

00:18:58.600 --> 00:18:59.960
Isn't it obvious?!

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:03.600
It feels good to be surrounded by beauties!

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:05.840
Beauties...?

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:06.830
Just look at her.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.380
She's delicate, yet has a perfectly 
balanced linear beauty

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.790
like the willowy waist of a holy maiden!

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:18.590
Meanwhile, this one has a bewitching mix
of refined dignity and dangerous mystique.

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:23.150
She's as pristine and beautiful as any flower,
 with an edge as white as lilies themselves.

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:28.670
Sorry. My master here is the kind of pervert

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:32.010
who prefers Kitetsu Blades over 
having three meals a day.

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:32.860
Are you okay?

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:36.530
Aw, are you trying to flatter me?

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.040
Hey, who are you guys?!

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:49.870
Just some dogs for hire 
without names worth sharing.

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:51.220
Dogs?

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:54.040
Musashi!

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:54.900
Hey, guys!

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:56.350
An oni showed up, right?

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:57.550
Where's my sword?!

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:58.980
Are you okay?

00:19:58.980 --> 00:19:59.970
There it is!

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:02.230
Those people lent me a sword, 
and I took care of...

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:04.120
Wait, the sword's gone!

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.320
Say, what people are you talking about?

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:10.340
They vanished...

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.120
Are you sure you weren't dreaming?

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.610
I know I wasn't!

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.780
That sword was so awesome...

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:23.230
It was like something 
from out of this world!

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:26.960
I can't wait to use a Kitetsu Blade again!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.670
And what exactly is a Kitetsu Blade?

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:32.550
I mean, a Kitetsu Blade is...

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:35.850
Huh, I don't actually know.

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:38.050
You seriously don't?

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:42.000
It's one of these. A blade made from Kitetsu.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.350
Your swords are made of Kitetsu, Tsugumi?!

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.070
Of course they are.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:48.810
You can't break an oni's horn 
without a Kitetsu Blade.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:50.520
For real?!

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.680
Yeah. Their horns are super hard,

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:57.950
so you can't break them 
without the special power of Kitetsu.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:01.560
The only thing that can finish off an oni...

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:05.150
They're bound to be rare, 
and valuable as weapons ago.

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:09.500
I bet it's gonna be some kind of 
epic quest to get our hands on—

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:10.320
Just buy one.

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:13.160
People sell 'em, y'know.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.900
Where?! Where do we get them?!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:24.220
When a Kishin shows up, 
Bushi aren't far behind to slay it.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:28.400
And not long after that come merchants
looking to do business with the Bushi.

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:30.810
Equipment, liquor, food, 
and information are all for sale...

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:33.900
Even Kitetsu Blades.

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:35.600
Awesome!

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:39.490
Maybe this would be a good 
place to prepare for battle.

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:40.860
They're a must-have!

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:43.930
You can't beat a Kishin 
without a Kitetsu Blade.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:48.440
All righty! Guess we're gonna do a 
little shopping before our oni hunt!

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:52.490
Shopping, shopping! 
Shopping for Kitetsu Blades!

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:54.160
Do we have any money...?

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:28.130
You really do know your stuff, 
Tsugumi! I'm impressed!

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:31.010
Yeah. With you around, I think our 
trip's gonna be a lot smoother.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:32.360
Tsugumi the smarty!

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:34.490
Aw, I'm nothing special...

00:23:34.490 --> 00:23:35.500
You embarrassed?

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:36.790
You look freaky like that!

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:39.850
I took so much verbal abuse growing up, 
I don't know how to react to praise...

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Next Time
You Can't Survive Underwater</b>
